From d52cf1c86a6d3834cb9001a43663cc6ace03986d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 10:41:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 238/239] ipa: rkisp2: Add the spatial noise reduction and
 sharpening

The ISPP NR and SHP stages run on whatever the static Ispp parameters
hold, which for every tuning so far is nothing: both stages process
each frame with all-zero parameters.

Add a NoiseReduction algorithm for the luma wavelet (YNR) and chroma
(UVNR) filters of the NR block and a Sharpen algorithm for the
sharpening and edge filters of the SHP block. Both interpolate a per
ISO step calibration at the gain of the latest ISP frame and convert
it the way the Rockchip AIQ does, at unity strength, so that the IQ
calibration of a sensor applies as is. NoiseReduction follows the
gain ratio and gain map use of TemporalNoiseReduction. The NR and SHP
blocks move out of the static Ispp parameters.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
